				\begin{document}$$d_{\textrm{w}}$$\end{document}  is difficult. To quantify the quality of the manufactured spot welds, various methods for non-destructive testing (NDT) and destructive testing (DT) are used. Manual ultrasonic testing is the most frequently used NDT method for RSW. This is made clear in DVS technical bulletin 2916-5 [ 1 ], as the low relevance of all other methods for RSW is pointed out. Until now, all available NDT methods are of an indirect kind. They always require a reference or comparison value to evaluate the results and must be validated and calibrated. Standardized DT methods are generally used for this purpose. A distinction can be made between workshop and laboratory testing methods. In the workshop tests, the samples are clamped in a vice and destroyed using a hammer or a pair of pliers, for example. The weld diameter  d w \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
