In the present study, two material combinations (MC) are selected for the analysis with different elongations  A 80, resulting in spot welds with different ductility, leading to either ductile (MC1) or brittle (MC2) fractures. MC1 consists of two sheets of galvanized CR300LA GI40/40 steel. MC2 consists of two hot-stamped steel sheets manufactured from a 22MnB5+AS150 alloy with an aluminum-silicon coating. The mechanical material properties are listed in Table  2 . Each MC consists of two sheets of the same thickness. Three distinct sheet thicknesses have been selected for MC1 and MC2, as indicated by the respective MC-IDs in Table  3 . The welding parameters were selected with the objective of preventing expulsions, which would otherwise result in an unstable nugget diameter size for the spot weld within each MC. A minimum of ten samples is welded for each MC-ID. All MCs and the welding parameters are shown in Table  3 . The welding parameters are determined in advance on the basis of weldability lobes. The samples are welded with a servo-electric  C -type welding gun, with a stiffness of  k = 2.345 k N m - 1 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
